<title>SPAIN: Spain's BCH sells 45.8 percent of Azucarera.</title>
<headline>Spain's BCH sells 45.8 percent of Azucarera.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Central Hispano has sold 24 percent of sugar group Azucarera de Espana to Caja de Salamanca y Soria and a further 21.8 percent to Ebro Agricolas, the CNMV stock market commission said.</p>
<p>The price of the sale was 5,215 pesetas per share.</p>
<p>BCH announced in September it was planning to sell its 49.9 percent stake in Azucarera. It was not clear on Monday whether it still owned the remaining 4.1 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
